  "created": "2026-11-27T20:37:03.687Z",
  "description": "EvoPdf Next PDF Processor for .NET (Multi-platform) can be used to extract text and images from PDF documents, convert PDF documents to Markdown, search text in PDF documents and convert PDF pages to images.\n\nThe package includes the PDF to Text, PDF to Markdown, PDF to Image and PDF Images Extractor components.\n\nThe library targets .NET Standard 2.0 and can be used in .NET Core and .NET Framework applications deployed on Windows, Linux and macOS, including Azure, AWS, Google Cloud, Docker and Kubernetes.\n\nThis multi-platform metapackage installs the Windows x64 and Linux x64 runtimes.\n\nFor Windows ARM64, Linux ARM64 and macOS ARM64, the additional packages EvoPdf.Next.PdfProcessor.Windows.Arm64, EvoPdf.Next.PdfProcessor.Linux.Arm64 and EvoPdf.Next.PdfProcessor.MacOS can be referenced on their own or alongside this package.\n\nCompatibility:\n\n* Windows 10, 11 and Windows Server 2016 to 2025 (x64)\n* Linux (x64) - Debian 11+, Ubuntu 20.04+ or equivalent\n* Windows, Linux and macOS (ARM64) - via additional packages\n* .NET 11.0, 10.0, 9.0, 8.0, 7.0, 6.0 and .NET Standard 2.0\n* .NET Framework 4.6.2 to 4.8.1\n* Azure, AWS and Google Cloud\n* Virtual Machines\n* Docker containers and Kubernetes\n* Web, Console and Desktop applications\n\nMain Features:\n\n* Convert PDF documents to text preserving the original layout or optimized for reading\n* Search text in PDF documents and return the exact positions of the matches\n* Convert PDF documents to Markdown with headings, lists, tables, links and images\n* Convert PDF pages to PNG images using a specified color space\n* Extract images from PDF documents in PNG format preserving transparency\n* Process password-protected PDF documents\n* Process all PDF pages or a specified range of PDF pages\n\nDocumentation and code samples:\nhttps://www.evopdf.com/evopdf-next-pdf-processor-dotnet",
  "iconFile": "images\\icon.png",
